# Images the monitor must not publish by itself (upstream-check.yml).
#
# Empty (comments only) in normal operation. To freeze an image while a bad
# release is investigated or rolled back, add a line with `resolver` or
# `sidecar`, through a pull request. While an image is listed here:
#   * no new Unbound version, base image or rescan result publishes it;
#   * its base digests in .build-state.json stay as they are;
#   * its current release is not re-dispatched or repaired;
#   * `gh workflow run upstream-check.yml -f rebuild=<image>` still publishes
#     a new revision, built from exactly what the repository pins.
# An issue stays open for as long as something is listed.
# Procedure: docs/operations.md, "Rolling back a release".
